## Fatigue

MS fatigue is not like normal tiredness. Plan your day, **pace yourself**, take rests before you need them, and prioritise what matters.

## Heat

Heat, from hot weather, hot baths or exercise, can make symptoms worse for a while. Cooling vests, fans and cool drinks help.

## Exercise

Exercise is safe and helps strength, balance, fatigue and mood. A physiotherapist can suggest what suits you.

## Healthy living

- **stop smoking**, as smoking can make MS progress faster
- eat a balanced diet
- ask your team about **vitamin D**

## Pregnancy

Many people with MS have children. Talk to your team before trying for a baby, as some treatments need to be stopped or changed.

## Driving

You must tell the **DVLA** if you have MS. Many people can carry on driving, sometimes with adaptations.

## Support

The **MS Society** and **MS Trust** both have free helplines and information.
